+# Privacy-safe CLI feedback
+
+## Intent
+
+Add the smallest private feedback path that can persist an allowlisted Forge-owned
+failure locally, preview exactly what will be sent, and transmit it only after
+explicit interactive approval.
+
+## Locked decisions
+
+- Consent is local and is exactly `disabled`, `pending`, or `enabled`; it is never
+  implicitly enabled.
+- Only fixed, structured Forge failure fields are accepted. Prompts, code, diffs,
+  paths, logs, arguments, environment, secrets, and identity fields have no input
+  or payload slot.
+- Non-interactive execution never prompts or sends. Pending drafts can be handled
+  by a later interactive `forge feedback` invocation.
+- A declined incident deletes its draft and suppresses only its fingerprint.
+  Global disable deletes all drafts and the anonymous source ID.
+- The client is deterministic and uses no model/provider token. The transport is
+  native HTTPS with an injectable endpoint and client for tests.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+Backend AI triage, public issue promotion, analytics/clustering services, free-form
+descriptions, repository identity, and any user model/provider integration.
+
+## Ambiguity policy
+
+Fail closed. Do not capture an unknown failure code, do not send without an HTTPS
+endpoint and explicit approval, and do not add fields beyond the fixed schema.
